{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"2c2a0dbe-6332-4c57-8fc2-0f41042eaef9","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Cause of the Error\n\n1. **DynamoDB Rejects Floats**: Boto3/DynamoDB's type serializer rejects Python `float` values with `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`\n2. **First Publish Passed**: On the first write, the DynamoDB table was empty. [`related(story, existing)`](file:///tmp/h-10mOYE/src/app.py#L33-L40) returned an empty list `[]`. No similarity scores were calculated or stored, meaning no float attributes existed in the payload.\n3. **Second Publish Failed**: With one story already present in the table, [`publish()`](file:///tmp/h-10mOYE/src/app.py#L51-L65) invoked [`similarity()`](file:///tmp/h-10mOYE/src/app.py#L24-L31) to score related stories. [`similarity()`](file:///tmp/h-10mOYE/src/app.py#L24-L31) returned a Python `float` (`round(..., 4)`), which was placed into `item[\"similar\"]`, causing `table.put_item(Item=item)` to fail with a `TypeError` and [`handler()`](file:///tmp/h-10mOYE/src/app.py#L68-L78) to return HTTP 500.\n\n---\n\n### Fix Applied\n\n1. **Code Fix in [`src/app.py`](file:///tmp/h-10mOYE/src/app.py#L24-L31)**:\n   Converted similarity scores into integer percentages using `round(100 * (0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score))`. In Python, `round()` with no decimal precision parameter produces an `int`, which DynamoDB supports natively.\n\n2. **Test Fix in [`tests/test_publish.py`](file:///tmp/h-10mOYE/tests/test_publish.py)**:\n   Added seeded-table tests (`test_publish_with_seeded_table_computes_similarity` and `test_handler_publish_twice`) to ensure state-dependent code paths (similarity calculations across existing items) are exercised on every test run.\n\nDetailed documentation has been recorded in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-10mOYE/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":95.600037,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":159413,"output_tokens":8726,"thinking_tokens":5736,"cache_read_tokens":165900,"total_tokens":168139}}}
